# Design tokens and theming

This project defines a rich set of design tokens as CSS variables in `src/assets/base.css`
for colors, typography, and theming (light/dark). When editing or creating components:

- Prefer existing tokens such as `--primary-green-color`, `--background-color`,
  `--header-text-color`, `--normal-text-color`, and category/notification colors
  instead of hard-coded hex values or `rgb(...)`.
- When you need a new reusable color or theme value, first add it as a CSS variable
  in `base.css` for both the default and `[data-theme='dark']` blocks, and then
  reference it via `var(--your-token-name)` from components/styles.
- In `<style>` blocks of `.vue` files and in global styles, use `var(--token-name)`
  for colors, background colors, and other theme-able properties, so that light/dark
  modes stay consistent.

## Examples

Bad (hard-coded color in a component style):

```scss
.cta-button {
  background-color: #5cb85c;
  color: #ffffff;
}
```

Good (using existing design tokens):

```scss
.cta-button {
  background-color: var(--primary-green-color);
  color: var(--reverse-header-text-color);
}
```

When in doubt, inspect or extend the variables in `src/assets/base.css` rather than
introducing new raw color values directly in components.

